        "\n",
        "In this section, we will give you all the essential information to correctly start using the `reflectance` package.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 1. **Do you have reflectance data files?**\n",
        "\n",
        "The whole package is based on reflectance data files that you either obtained yourself when performing reflectance measurements or obtained from someone else. Each file corresponds to a single measurement and consists of an excel file with a specific structure organizing the data inside the file. Check the [datafiles section](datafiles.qmd) for more information about the data files. \n",
        "\t\n",
        "If you don't have any reflectance files, the package has a function to load reflectance files, so that you can use these files to play with the functionalities of the package (see [get_datasets](https://g-patin.github.io/reflectance/get_datasets/) section).  \n",
        "\t\n",
        "If you have files, there are many possibilities to select and encapsulate your local files inside a python list object. I will show only one of the methods for which I will use the `glob` package.\n",
        "&nbsp;"
      ],
      "id": "8df9b9ca"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# I use this package to select files on my local computer\n",
        "from glob import glob "
      ],
      "id": "e2996790",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
