        "## 2. **Central role of the `RS` class**\n",
        "\n",
        "Once you have selected reflectance files and encapsulated them inside a python list, you will need to create an instance of the `RS` class passing the variable for your reflectance files as argument (see code below). Most of the functions provided by the package can only be accessed through the `RS` class.  \n",
        "&nbsp;\n"
      ],
      "id": "aefe62a1"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import reflectance as rf"
      ],
      "id": "a4d95d83",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import reflectance as rf\n",
        "files = rf.get_datasets(device='AVT',rawfiles=False)\n",
        "rs = rf.RS(files=files)\n",
        "print(files)"
      ],
      "id": "f772fb57",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
